  "ingredients": [
    "1 1/2 ounce cheddar cheese",
    "105 gram cauliflower (riced)",
    "3 tablespoon parmesan cheese (shredded)",
    "2 large egg",
    "4 tablespoon almond flour",
    "1/4 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/4 teaspoon onion powder",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "4 ounce bacon",
    "4 ounce ground beef (70/30)",
    "4 tablespoon low-carb bbq sauce",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "1 1/2 ounce cheddar cheese (shredded)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Slice the bacon into thin strips and pan fry over medium-high heat. Once the bacon is partially cooked, add in the beef and cook until crispy.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/IMG_8388.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shred the cheddar cheese by hand or in a food processor. Set aside. Measure out the cauliflower crumbles using a scale or measuring cup. Mix in half of the cheddar cheese. Next, add the parmesan, eggs, almond flour, and spices. Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/IMG_8379.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add any excess grease from the pan into the waffle mixture. Using an immersion blender, blend the waffle mixture into a thick paste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/IMG_8397.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add half of the mixture to the waffle iron and cook until crisp. Keep in mind that cauliflower waffles tend to take a little bit longer to cook (there's much more moisture). A good rule of thumb to use is that the waffle is finished once there is little to no steam coming from the waffle iron. Repeat for the remaining waffles.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/IMG_8407.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the waffles are cooking, add the sugar-free BBQ sauce to the bacon and ground beef mixture in the pan. Season well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/IMG_8415.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Assemble the waffles with the ground beef mixture and shredded cheese on top. Broil for 1–2 minutes or until the cheese is melted.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/IMG_8424.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve hot and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/bbq-bacon-cheeseburger-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51915-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
